{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5FUP2NX4B44chtBmSu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `addMonths` in `dates.js`. Customers billed on the 31st will now land on the last day of shorter months instead of rolling into the following month.\n\nThe bug was that `setMonth` doesn't clamp. Jan 31 + 1 month became \"Feb 31\", which rolls over to Mar 3. The fix moves the date to the 1st before changing the month, then clamps the original day to the last day of the target month.\n\nI checked it with Node:\n- Jan 31 2026 09:30 + 1 month → Feb 28 2026 09:30 (time of day kept)\n- Jan 15 2026 + 1 month → Feb 15 2026 (unchanged)\n- Jan 31 2024 + 1 month → Feb 29 2024 (leap year)\n- Mar 31 2026 − 1 month → Feb 28 2026\n- Jan 31 2026 + 13 months → Feb 28 2027\n\nThe folder isn't a git repo and I didn't run any test suite, since I didn't find one. Any billing code that relied on the old overflow behavior will now see different dates for month-end anchors."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1139,"cache_read_input_tokens":23254,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1139},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1938e635-7b90-4f57-b7ee-e2327202d8f9","uuid":"b0f82e3a-73c2-4ec7-9e68-21781531b154","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:30:47.913Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5FUCrCXngKh7eLeyHE"}
